From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Rogers <pdr@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:14:43 -0700
Subject: [html-in-canvas] Disallow canvas-external SVG filters

This patch prevents elements in a canvas subtree from referencing SVG
`<filter>` elements outside the canvas subtree, similar to
https://crrev.com/c/8455562. Previously,
`FilterEffectBuilder::BuildReferenceFilter` did not check
`IsInCanvasSubtree()` on the target `SVGFilterElement`, allowing CSS
`filter`, CSS `backdrop-filter`, and SVG `filter` references to leak
external state such as `:visited` styles.

`FilterEffectBuilder` now accepts `is_in_canvas_subtree` from
`PaintLayer` and `SVGElementResourceClient`, ignoring external
`<filter>` elements when set. `SVGElement` and `SVGFilterElement` also
invalidate cached filter state in `DidChangeIsInCanvasSubtree`.
Existing `drawElementImage` filter tests that placed allowed `<filter>`
elements outside `<canvas>` are updated to define them inside
`<canvas>`.

Fixed: 576312229
Change-Id: I5174e5ac783667d18535cee8fd30ca8dbc596849
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8615847
Commit-Queue: Philip Rogers <pdr@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Stephen Chenney <schenney@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1726439}

Electron adaptation notes (45-x-y): every conflict was in third_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt (html-in-canvas privacy WPTs whose branch versions predate upstream's later edits, plus filtered-div-drawable-added-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html which the branch does not have); the branch's test files are kept and that test is not carried. The fix's svg_element.cc / svg_resources.cc / paint code hunks applied cleanly. Build fix folded in: the branch's Element::DidChangeIsInCanvasSubtree() takes no CanvasSubtreePropagation argument (added upstream later), so the new SVGElement / SVGFilterElement overrides and their base-class calls use the parameterless signature.

